{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1345214-physical-goddess-spiritual-goddess","id":1345214,"title":"Physical goddess, Spiritual goddess","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-11-01T06:21:58-07:00","id":1345214,"title":"Physical goddess, Spiritual goddess","content":"<b>Executive Summary:</b> I\u2019m trying to imagine how a physical immortal who inspired and currently is masquerading as a deity interacts with the spirit who grew into an emulation of that deity.<br /> <br /> So, I\u2019ve got a mortal-centered game set on a fictional British island (fill in the space between Guernsey and Jersey). The setting is very gothic-countryside, with many of the locals believing in and sometimes even worshiping the goddess of their pre-Celtic forebears. (This is the same setting as the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/799082-cofd-diy-mystery-cults/page4\">Janlarek mystery cult</a><br /> <br /> Unbeknownst to them, the goddess was originally a vampire who did what vampires do\u2014plaguing some people, elevating a few, and being mysterious. When she awoke from slumber, she had become a legend, and carefully cultivated her image to become the local goddess.<br /> <br /> Centuries passed, and she continued to exist in the shadows, occasionally helping or hindering the local people in such a way as to maintain belief. Gradually, she forgot her former life; she had become this goddess, helping her people, protecting her land, but not necessarily meddling with individual lives. She made things difficult for missionaries, and aided the partisans when the Germans came. Vampires and werewolves have never settled in her territory. <br /> <br /> I\u2019ve been thinking about this land in the Shadow, and the spirits that would follow her like ravens to feed on the Essence her actions bring. Perhaps one spirit, a doppleganger Goddess, would arise in more or less the vampire\u2019s form. Maybe it shadows her, maybe it tries to take control of her. Maybe it seeks to up the visibility of the deity in order to garner more Essence, which would upset the vampire\u2019s low-key method of operating. Would they operate in tandem, with mutual awareness? Would the vampire even know the spirit exists, or would she believe any of the positive spiritual happenstances were merely products of her own supernatural influence?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T11:31:12-07:00","id":1345283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corrigan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1345214-physical-goddess-spiritual-goddess#post1345214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019ve been thinking about this land in the Shadow, and the spirits that would follow her like ravens to feed on the Essence her actions bring. Perhaps one spirit, a doppleganger Goddess, would arise in more or less the vampire\u2019s form. Maybe it shadows her, maybe it tries to take control of her. Maybe it seeks to up the visibility of the deity in order to garner more Essence, which would upset the vampire\u2019s low-key method of operating. Would they operate in tandem, with mutual awareness? Would the vampire even know the spirit exists, or would she believe any of the positive spiritual happenstances were merely products of her own supernatural influence?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe the spirits would be more likely to hang around the people. While the vampire may be inspiring it, they are the source of it, so the lions share of the Essence would come from them. And once powerful enough yes, they or one among them that managed to grow the most powerful, would start influencing the vampire and make it do more. And later flat out Claim them.<br /> <br /> The vampire would likely not know the spirits exist, as they have no inherent way to notice the Shadow or even Twilight, but if they are really skilled with Auspex or know Cruac they might get some idea of things. <br /> <br /> For more Shadow-stuff you might check out Werewolf books, specifically Predators, or the blue Book of the Spirits. Both are first edition but for the most part the setting information transfers over without change. Shunned by the Moon, a new release that focuses on antagonists, also introduces an idigam who seeks to be a god and the troubles it has when granting miracles (notably, when you start just answering prayers, faith goes down, as you're dealing more in an exchange like a merchant/customer relationship).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T16:48:40-07:00","id":1345349,"title":"","content":"I think it could be interesting if the spirit-goddess had a Ban that prevented her from acknowledging or perceiving the material one. That way, you get two goddesses believing themselves one, working at cross purposes while simultaneously strengthening each others' positions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-02T09:00:57-07:00","id":1345442,"title":"","content":"I love this idea - and it's very similar to something I've run in the past. Both <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar97_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"97\" data-vbnamecard=\"97\">The MG</a> have solid takes on this; without a ban similar to what The MG suggests, I imagine that the end result you can expect is for the Spirit goddess to end up claiming the vampire. If you want to keep them as separate entities, then I would definitely go with the ban; due to the way vampire works, the vampire would already be largely ignorant of the spirit, this just enforces it both ways and lets you extend the drama of having both for far longer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-03T15:13:24-08:00","id":1345653,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the input!<br /> <br /> My initial thought was to have the vampire learn Blood Tenebrous at some point, and then go about policing the local spirit world to suit her (if she could feed on Essence, that would allow her to stay fed without other vampires in the vicinity). That would be the easy way to do it, but I\u2019m not sure it would be the most interesting way.<br /> <br /> Part of me wants the vampire to get claimed, but I think the Ban may be the way to go, just to keep things in an odd tension of balance.<br /> <br /> A friend suggested that one of the witches might be able to sense spirits and is visited by the spirit goddess; that witch forms a heretical splinter faction of the cult who believes the rest of the group worships a false version. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}